<section class="section section-tight">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section-title section-title-glow section-title-center">Section-by-section optimization guide</h2>
    <div class="two-col-grid" style="margin-top:28px;">
      <div class="content-panel">
        <h3>1. Headline (220 characters)</h3>
        <p>The most important field for recruiter search visibility. LinkedIn's algorithm weights your headline heavily. Formula: <strong>[Level + Title] | [Specialization] | [Value or targeting signal]</strong></p>
        <ul class="checklist">
          <li>Include your exact target role title</li>
          <li>Include 2–3 domain or technology keywords</li>
          <li>Use all 220 characters — do not leave space unused</li>
          <li>Do not just list your current employer</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 style="margin-top:24px;">2. About section (150–300 words)</h3>
        <p>Four parts: identity, outcomes, specialization, targeting. First line must hook before "see more." Write in first person. End with a specific targeting statement.</p>
        <ul class="checklist">
          <li>Opens with your level + role + domain</li>
          <li>Includes 2–3 quantified outcomes</li>
          <li>Names your specific specialization</li>
          <li>Closes with what you are looking for</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 style="margin-top:24px;">3. Experience section</h3>
        <p>Each role: accurate job title (how LinkedIn categorizes you), 3–5 quantified bullets. Do not copy your resume verbatim — LinkedIn allows more narrative. Include keywords from your target job descriptions.</p>
        <ul class="checklist">
          <li>Job title field matches your actual seniority</li>
          <li>Every bullet has a quantified outcome where possible</li>
          <li>Keywords from target postings appear naturally</li>
          <li>Start date and end date filled in for every role</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 style="margin-top:24px;">4. Skills section (50 skills)</h3>
        <p>Fill to capacity. LinkedIn uses your Skills section heavily in search ranking. Endorsed skills carry additional weight — ask 5–10 colleagues to endorse your top skills.</p>
        <ul class="checklist">
          <li>50 skills listed (maximum)</li>
          <li>Top 3 pinned skills are your highest-priority keywords</li>
          <li>At least 5–10 skills have endorsements</li>
          <li>Skills match keywords from target job descriptions exactly</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="content-panel">
        <h3>5. Featured section</h3>
        <p>The Featured section appears above your About section and is often the first content a recruiter scrolls to after your headline. Link to portfolio work, published articles, GitHub, or a specific project showcase.</p>
        <ul class="checklist">
          <li>At least one Featured item added</li>
          <li>Links to relevant proof of work (portfolio, GitHub, published content)</li>
          <li>Featured items have descriptive titles and custom thumbnails if possible</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 style="margin-top:24px;">6. Open to Work settings</h3>
        <p>Recruiter-only mode signals availability without alerting your current employer. Be specific — vague settings produce irrelevant outreach.</p>
        <ul class="checklist">
          <li>Specific target job titles listed (not "open to anything")</li>
          <li>Locations set correctly (including Remote if applicable)</li>
          <li>Start date reflects genuine availability</li>
          <li>Recruiter-only mode enabled (not public banner)</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 style="margin-top:24px;">7. Recommendations</h3>
        <p>Three to five strong, specific recommendations from managers and senior collaborators. Each recommendation should name a specific project and include an observable or quantified outcome.</p>

        <h3 style="margin-top:24px;">8. Contact and basic info</h3>
        <ul class="checklist">
          <li>Custom LinkedIn URL (linkedin.com/in/yourname)</li>
          <li>Email address visible to connections</li>
          <li>Website or portfolio link in contact info</li>
          <li>Industry and location fields set correctly</li>
          <li>Pronouns set if desired</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 style="margin-top:24px;">9. Education and certifications</h3>
        <ul class="checklist">
          <li>All relevant degrees listed with institution and graduation year</li>
          <li>Relevant certifications listed (AWS, PMP, CFA, CPA, etc.)</li>
          <li>GPA included if 3.5+ and graduated within last 5 years</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

